{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools","id":1015674,"title":"Examples of magical tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T08:00:52-08:00","id":1015674,"title":"Examples of magical tools","content":"For inspiration / examples sake, could I see some lists of magical tools that some your characters use / keep on hand? I'm having trouble getting a practical grip on them. Do any Acanthuses (Acathi? Acanthese? Acanthodes? Acanthae? do they follow the plant conventions?) actually carry a glass or silver wand around with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:39:38-08:00","id":1015703,"title":"","content":"Sure, it's one of their Path tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:56:16-08:00","id":1015706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools#post1015674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For inspiration / examples sake, could I see some lists of magical tools that some your characters use / keep on hand? I'm having trouble getting a practical grip on them. Do any Acanthuses (Acathi? Acanthese? Acanthodes? Acanthae? do they follow the plant conventions?) actually carry a glass or silver wand around with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acanthi. And yeah - glass rods, silver coins, mirrors, crystal wine glasses, (or maybe chrome flasks for something more portable), stiletto knives... PathTools are literally just coins, cups, mirrors, rods, and weapons made of the appropriate material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-11-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:39:33-08:00","id":1015730,"title":"","content":"Not all path tools might be viable to carry around but most Mages could carry at least some around.<br /> Coins are quite easy since all paths have materials that can be made into coins.<br /> Everyone can keep cups at home, but if you want to you could carry canteens made out of leather, steel or wood. Hip flasks are usually stainless steel, but historically they've also been made out of silver and even glass.<br /> Mirrors are usually made out of glass or sometimes silver, but brass, steel and copper can all be polished and used as mirrors.<br /> Wands can be made from almost any solid materials and they don't have to be long.<br /> Weapons are a bit trickier, but not impossible to carry even if you're going to interact with sleeper society. Everyone can carry a knife made out of the right material if their clothes are baggy enough or if they carry a purse/backpack. Otherwise Obrimos and Thyrsus has the better chance of getting away with carrying a small steel pocket knife or a sling respectively.<br /> <br /> But I think it's a bit more common to use path tools in the privacy of your home. The Yantra bonus is quite small so you'd only want to use them if you have a free Yantra slot during your ritual casting.<br /> <br /> Edit: What does &quot;worked materials&quot; mean for Mastigoi? Can they use any kind of paper currency as a representation for coins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-11-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:56:23-08:00","id":1015792,"title":"","content":"My Moros Adamantine Arrow used the following magical tools:<br /> A WWII tactical knife (Order tool)<br /> An ashwood pentacle (Path tool)<br /> Gloves (Matter tool)<br /> Bullet used to murder her father (Death tool)<br /> <br /> My Mastigos Adamantine Arrow used:<br /> Brass knuckles (Order tool)<br /> Wrought Iron Pentacle (Path tool)<br /> Mirror Shard (Mind magic)<br /> Zippo lighter (Forces magic)<br /> Black rope (Space magic)<br /> Furthermore ... all of his magical tools are things he stole.<br /> <br /> My Acanthus used a stained glass Pentacle... look up the icon for the Changeling the Dreaming Art of Wayfare. That's what I used as the image for her magical tool related to her path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:16:24-08:00","id":1015842,"title":"","content":"My Thyrsus Thearch (in training) uses the following regularly:<br /> <br /> -A metal Army canteen (Path Tool; Dedicated Tool)<br /> -Sacred pools (and water in general) (Extended from canteen as a Path Tool)<br /> -Fossilized shark tooth necklace (Commonly used in divination and Spirit-related spells)<br /> -Hand-made clay and wood masks (Purpose-made for shapeshifting into specific forms)<br /> <br /> Included in this also is the Persona Yantra for Morrigan Leighis; aiding in spells that let them heal, change shape, or command spirits.<br /> <br /> And my players in other games...<br /> <br /> Moros Mystagogue:<br /> <br /> -A gold coin (minted himself; bears the image of a dragon wearing a crown) (Path Tool; Dedicated Tool)<br /> -Alchemical concoctions (Matter/Life spells related to altering, restoring, or harming the target they're applied to)<br /> <br /> Included in this is the Persona Yantra of Midas the King Wyrm; empowering spells related to commanding action, which includes commanding objects.<br /> <br /> Obrimos Thearch:<br /> <br /> -Mathematical equations (Path Tool; Dedicated Tool)<br /> -Technological devices (Forces/Mind spells)<br /> -High Speech (deserves special note for its frequency of use)<br /> <br /> No persona for this one, but goes by the Shadow Name of Ash.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Worth adding is the magical philosophies behind each.<br /> <br /> Morrigan's magical philosophy doesn't articulate or analogize too strongly and operates heavily off of feeling. She often describes the ecstasy of her magic, though, as like water flowing into a vessel, and the vessel constraining it; giving it shape. As such, a lot of yantras are about giving magic the right vessel to flow into; into a target's wounds, into the world itself, or, far more often, into the Thyrsus herself. The yantras act as, or change, the vessel, and thus change the resulting magic.<br /> <br /> Midas sees magic as a form of alchemy; internal and external. Mana is the prima materiae, and the arcana are that which give it form; bending and creating reality by transforming the raw, primordial Mana. The arcana themselves are willful, as Mysterium philosophy purports, and bend and reshape the world in accordance with their natures. The gold coin he carries is his own imprinting of his will on the world.<br /> <br /> Ash sees the universe in equations; everything the output of narrow, deterministic processes. He does not believe in the Copenhagen Interpretation; he is a sincerely Einsteinean physicist first and foremost. By understanding and unlocking these high equations and using his soul as a kind of Supernal field generator, he can bend reality; rewrite the equations locally. The more he understands, the more potent his understanding becomes.<br /> <br /> Ash would've been a libertine if he didn't think they were all a bunch of wankers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:33:05-08:00","id":1015873,"title":"","content":"I had an Obrimos who used a steel pen for a wand. It was easy to carry and not even security guards at the airport gave it a second glance. You could usually get away with holding it in hand without looking out of place. A pen can be made of just about any material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T16:33:00-08:00","id":1015891,"title":"","content":"I generally allow my players to use Magical Tools that incorporate the appropriate materials in their design, not just tools that are made entirely out of them.<br /> <br /> An Acanthus might have an old gnarled staff that has a crystal mounted at it's tip. An Obrimos might have a golden coin. A Mastigos might have a mirror mounted in an ornate iron stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T17:59:20-08:00","id":1016339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1015842#post1015842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Mathematical equations (Path Tool; Dedicated Tool)<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware that something like that could be a path tool. Is it a home rule?<br /> To everyone - I didn't think Arcana tools exited in 2e. Are they mentioned somewhere in the book?<br /> Come to think of it, I don't think I specified 2e, so maybe that isn't pertinent to you examples.<br /> In any case, thanks to everyone who responded. This was helpful.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T18:04:52-08:00","id":1016341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1016339#post1016339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware that something like that could be a path tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't, though a Libertine could probably use it as an Order tool with Techne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1016339#post1016339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To everyone - I didn't think Arcana tools exited in 2e. Are they mentioned somewhere in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Just Path Tools and Order Tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T18:33:49-08:00","id":1016348,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin is right; he technically shouldn't have been allowed to use equations as a Path Tool. However, given that he was an Obrimos physicist, there just wasn't going to be any symbol more appropriate than that. It reflected a belief in a structured, ordered universe, which felt fitting for the Path.<br /> <br /> In all my games thus far, whether playing or running (almost always the latter), it's generally been allowed that the PCs can use most anything that is symbolically appropriate for a yantra, as long as it accords with their own general magical symbolism. It's something of a residue, though, since every single one of those games started before 2e was released. RAW, a Mage should only be allowed to use magical tools as determined by their Path, Order, or Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T18:47:15-08:00","id":1016351,"title":"","content":"A mathematical equation would fly as a Legacy Tool, that's the area I find a little confusing, Path Tools are a leftover from 1ed but Techne and Legacy tools are new to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:25:38-08:00","id":1016467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1015706#post1015706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Acanthi.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acanthus&quot; is both singular and plural; the Path names are modern versions of ancient Greek terms, but they've warped over time and don't follow their antecedents linguistic rules. The original Greek was Acanthos (pl Acanthoi). &quot;Acanthi&quot; is just... Wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T05:25:27-08:00","id":1016500,"title":"","content":"Mathematical equations might also be usable as a persona tool Yantra if the mage has an appropriate shadow name and the accompanying merit (p.104).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T05:30:36-08:00","id":1016502,"title":"","content":"Instead of coins other symbols of material wealth can be used. I like rings myself.<br /> <br /> For mirrors - cell phones with mirror screen protectors would work and cell phones with self-facing cameras might work as well. Or even phones with displays that include micromirrors in the display elements though you will probably have to have this custom made.<br /> <br /> Acanthus could use target or .22 pistols as weapons.<br /> Mastigos could use guns loaded with certain types of expanding ammo as weapons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","user":"The Demon Code","date":".  Added guns 12-13-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12754-the-demon-code","name":"The Demon Code","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T07:51:05-08:00","id":1016546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1016467#post1016467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acanthus&quot; is both singular and plural; the Path names are modern versions of ancient Greek terms, but they've warped over time and don't follow their antecedents linguistic rules. The original Greek was Acanthos (pl Acanthoi). &quot;Acanthi&quot; is just... Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's maybe worth noting that acanthus (with the -us) is actually the Latin spelling where acanthi would be the correct second declension plural. The Romans borrowed their fair share of words from the Greeks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:12:27-08:00","id":1016558,"title":"","content":"I've always used all the path names as plurals, or used the sub-titled nicknames.<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;Acanthusites,&quot; &quot;Acanthians,&quot; &quot;Acanthenesians,&quot; and &quot;Acanthenegians&quot; will be hilarious to drop on my players with no warning and a completely straight face, as if it's normal. Bonus points if I can do it in the same scene, in different sentences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:53:59-08:00","id":1016579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1016467#post1016467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Acanthus&amp;quot; is both singular and plural; the Path names are modern versions of ancient Greek terms, but they've warped over time and don't follow their antecedents linguistic rules. The original Greek was Acanthos (pl Acanthoi). &amp;quot;Acanthi&amp;quot; is just... Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Good to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:11:19-08:00","id":1016818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1016467#post1016467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Acanthus&amp;quot; is both singular and plural; the Path names are modern versions of ancient Greek terms, but they've warped over time and don't follow their antecedents linguistic rules. The original Greek was Acanthos (pl Acanthoi). &amp;quot;Acanthi&amp;quot; is just... Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I having badwrongfun if I use the Greek -oi plurals anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:15:14-08:00","id":1016820,"title":"","content":"Badwrongfun is for stupid people and writers who are much more precious about their games. You do what you want.<br /> <br /> You'll be <i>wrong</i>, but you'll be doing what you want, and no one will care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:06:31-08:00","id":1017070,"title":"","content":"It's okay to be wrong as long as you are wrong willingly, because it becomes right for your gametable. It's a difference between making an informed choice and ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T12:52:04-07:00","id":1262571,"title":"","content":"Been awhile since I necrod a thread but <br /> <br /> Mastigos Guardian: <br /> <br /> \u2022the hood of his jacket(which the storyteller counted as a worked material) for use in his veiling spells, through the action of pulling the hood up(order tool)<br /> <br /> \u2022A Brass compass(Space Focus)<br /> <br /> \u2022An old Iron Kriss Dagger (Path)<br /> <br /> My Thrysus Silver ladder<br /> <br /> \u2022Wooden staff/walking stick (path)<br /> <br /> \u2022His Game Warden badge (which the storyteller associated with hunting, order)<br /> <br /> \u2022A handmade stone arrowhead (for his more aggressive acts)<br /> <br /> My Obrimos Adamantine Arrow<br /> <br /> \u2022 Steel Pocket Knife (path)<br /> <br /> \u2022 A gold medal(a symbol of competition)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Steel Flip lighter (forces focus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T12:58:42-07:00","id":1262574,"title":"","content":"One time I saw a guy have his character use a Burger King crown in a pinch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T07:39:02-07:00","id":1262677,"title":"","content":"In one of my variant settings, my main characters (not the main characters, it's a collaborative setting) have for their dedicated tools a misericord, a double-faced hammer (Mjolnir-style), a scimitar, a hunting knife and a jian; it's rather violent world so carrying weapons is perfectly normal. They each use different symbols of wealth: a small gold nugget, a silver coin, a brass passage token, a large garnet, a copper coin. Their wands are mostly rods: garnet, crystal, ash and brass. The Obrimos uses a steel wand. Their mirrors are mostly normal hand mirrors, framed with suitable materials. The exceptions are the Obrimos, whose mirror is a small steel plate, and the Thyrsus, whose mirror is a piece of obsidian. Their cups are a crystal goblet, a brass cup, a garnet goblet, a steel bowl and a wooden cup. If you're wondering why the Moros uses garnet so much, it's because garnet is very, very easy to get in large quantities; it's been used as an abrasive for millennia in the form of garnet sand. Lodestone to separate the garnet, then Shaping to go from sand to solid. That's also how they get glass of sufficient quality for their mirrors, and the Acanthus gets crystal in amounts sufficient to make a goblet and a rod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T13:35:36-07:00","id":1262930,"title":"","content":"I look at it as the mage's dedicated tool(s) are something they have to be able to use frequently, or something subtle people expect to see.<br /> <br /> For a witch or warlock, Costume art should work. Pretty much anything you could find at a ren fair or costume shop without drawling eyes on the street.<br /> For alchemist, Have a chunk of metal on a necklace, or carry around some kind of key chain with a exotic (but not lethal) gas or liquid in it.<br /> For thaumaurges, A actual key should be all you need, and is right on the nose.<br /> For a shaman, a walking stick should work. So will being eccentric and have a bit of tooth or claw jewelry.<br /> <br /> For Death themes, People surely publicly comment on why a priest or nun is going around in a cassock or habit; However, It takes a real jerk or major mental issues make trouble over it.<br /> For Fate, Carry around some dice. It will be odd, but that's about it.<br /> For Forces, A service tech isn't going to be herranged for carrying around a multi-meter or flashlight. A simple ID with a magnetic strip might work.<br /> For Life, A simple cloth woven or charm bracelet might do. A nature or animal themed tattoo might even work.<br /> For Matter, How often do you have to take a wedding ring, or is anyone going to really question with you fidgeting with it?<br /> For Mind, A X-Files t-shirt or just a quarts necklace might do wonders.<br /> For Prime, Almost any ID or uniform of a military or public service should work.<br /> For Space, Again, a wedding band should work. A key chain on your belt with a picture of someplace or person (even if they have no connection to you) no one should comment on if you don't check it every three seconds.<br /> For Spirit, A tattoo or bit of jewelry of almost anything should do here too. There is a infinite number of spirits out there.<br /> For Time, The easiest of all, a wrist watch should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T22:54:12-07:00","id":1263009,"title":"","content":"For Forces, Space or Time, a smartphone or even an Apple Watch would do nicely. But it's important to recall that a mage can only have one dedicated tool at any given time, so a dedicated tool is apt to be a Path or Order tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T09:56:35-07:00","id":1263079,"title":"","content":"That is true. Most of my plans got shot down recently, but I plan ahead. I did and somewhat do plan on going out of my way to do character development.<br /> <br /> That is, not just having a stock tool that I thought up a character creation. Making it unique as the story goes. Not just the watch, but a watch that I used to as a brass knuckle in a last desperate move against a villain. A watch I bargained with changelings and travel to the Hedge for to find Fae designed clockwork parts. All in character all as the game plays out from the first session to the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T12:00:53-07:00","id":1263108,"title":"","content":"So, for tools like coins, what do you have to do with them? Stare at then while concentrating? Place them on a focal point of a pentacle or maybe even a leyline crossing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T14:01:06-07:00","id":1263126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1263108#post1263108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for tools like coins, what do you have to do with them? Stare at then while concentrating? Place them on a focal point of a pentacle or maybe even a leyline crossing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would use them in whatever way is symbolically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T04:56:17-07:00","id":1263181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1263108#post1263108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for tools like coins, what do you have to do with them? Stare at then while concentrating? Place them on a focal point of a pentacle or maybe even a leyline crossing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have two, lay them on the eyes of a corpse for Corpse Mask.<br /> <br /> Hold the coin in your mouth for Ghost Gate.<br /> <br /> Get someone else to give you a coin as payment for killing someone, for Amorality. (There was a Guardians oblation form 1e that was more or less, a symbolic representation of being given money to betray someone.)<br /> <br /> Burying the coin perhaps? Symbolic of hiding or maybe forgetting something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:03:55-07:00","id":1263225,"title":"","content":"Actions and placements doesn't matter that much for Tool Yantras. Remember that they should be possible to use during a single turn during which you can perform other reflexive actions and apply your Defense against attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:01:04-07:00","id":1263251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015674-examples-of-magical-tools?p=1263225#post1263225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actions and placements doesn't matter that much for Tool Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is an easy way to lend specific symbolism to a tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that they should be possible to use during a single turn during which you can perform other reflexive actions and apply your Defense against attacks. </div> </div> </div>I don't see the need to interpret it that strictly. There's not much benefit to taking longer other than it being a little easier to think of symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}